/* ===== aeo-report-coinflow ===== */

/* ============================================================
   SiQ Readout Skin - 02 - Ivory / Navy v2
   Supersedes 01_ivory-navy-solid.css. Same look, three defects fixed.
   01 is left in place untouched for comparison.

   CHANGED FROM 01, and why:

   1. The three *-soft tokens are NO LONGER declared here.
      01 set --danger-soft:#E5484D, --caution-soft:#FF7A00,
      --success-soft:#12B76A. Those tokens are not brand hues, they are
      background SURFACES, and the readouts hardcode light text on top
      of them:
          .hero {background:var(--danger-soft); color:#F5F7FA}
          .rowhi{background:var(--danger-soft); color:#F5F7FA}
      Re-pointing them at saturated brand colour dropped that text from
      16.17:1 to 3.65:1, and .hero .sub (#B8C5D6) to 2.24:1. Both fail
      WCAG AA. This is the same defect fixed in the AEO template on
      2026-08-26; skin 01 would have reintroduced it.
      Leaving them undeclared means each readout keeps its own value:
          AEO family      opaque dark hex   -> stays a dark anchor, 16:1
          Coinflow readout rgba(...,0.10)   -> tints the ivory ground
      Both are correct. DO NOT add these three tokens to a skin.

   2. .bridge and .attribution added to the navy re-scope. They use
      var(--surface) / var(--surface-2) and sit directly beneath
      navy-filled .leak cards, so under 01 they rendered as light boxes
      in the middle of a navy stack.

   3. The palette block now names [data-theme="light"] explicitly.
      Under 01 the theme toggle was silently inert: the skin's :root
      matched the file's [data-theme="light"] on specificity and won on
      source order. Ivory in both states is the intended look, so this
      is now deliberate rather than accidental. To restore the dark
      editorial look on the dark side, delete [data-theme="dark"] from
      the selector below.
   ============================================================ */

/* --- palette: ivory ground, solid brand, solid health tiers --- */
/* NOTE: no --danger-soft / --caution-soft / --success-soft here. See 1. */
/* SPECIFICITY NOTE, 2026-08-31. The AEO / Demand / Campaign / Full-Funnel /
   Marketing templates declare their palette on `body[data-theme="dark"]`,
   which is specificity (0,1,1). A bare `:root` is (0,1,0) and LOSES to it no
   matter how late it is injected. That is why those reports flipped to an
   ivory background while their text tokens stayed at dark-theme white, and
   why the Signal Assessment (which declares on `:root`) was the only file
   that skinned cleanly. Matching every shape below fixes all of them.
   Do not simplify this selector list. */
body:is([data-page="aeo-report-coinflow"]), body:where(:is([data-page="aeo-report-coinflow"]))[data-theme="dark"], body:where(:is([data-page="aeo-report-coinflow"]))[data-theme="light"], html:where(:has(body:is([data-page="aeo-report-coinflow"])))[data-theme="dark"], html:where(:has(body:is([data-page="aeo-report-coinflow"])))[data-theme="light"], body:where(:is([data-page="aeo-report-coinflow"]))[data-theme="dark"], body:where(:is([data-page="aeo-report-coinflow"]))[data-theme="light"] {
  --canvas: #EFE8D8; --surface: #FBF8F1; --surface-2: #E7DECB;
  --border: rgba(20,25,34,0.14); --border-strong: rgba(20,25,34,0.32);
  --text-primary: #14181F; --text-secondary: #46505F; --text-tertiary: #5A636F;
  --brand-blue: var(--siq-blue); --brand-orange: var(--siq-orange); --ink: #101722; --navy: var(--siq-ink);
  --success: #12B76A; --caution: #FF7A00; --danger: #E5484D; --track: #E1D7C4;
}

